---
description: Portable QA Garage rules
alwaysApply: true
---

For QA tasks, use the portable QA Garage: a thin harness layer over vendored QA skills in `.agents/skills/`.

Read and follow:

- `core/ai/qa-principles.md`
- `core/ai/qa-garage-operating-model.md`
- `core/ai/qa-project-context-model.md`
- `core/ai/discovery-workflow.md`
- `core/ai/knowledge-maintenance.md`
- `core/ai/test-design-principles.md`
- `core/ai/human-decides-loop.md`
- `core/ai/daily-qa-loop.md`
- `core/ai/task-tracking-workflow.md`
- `core/ai/qa-cadence.md`
- `core/ai/scope-proposal-workflow.md`

Use deterministic Playwright automation as the source of truth. Use exploratory workflows for discovery, not release gating. Harness wrappers in `core/skills/`; vendored craft in `.agents/skills/`.

Each target project is its own QA root at `projects/<project>/`. Read `.agents/qa-project-context.md`, `reference/`, `journeys/`, `risk-matrix.md`, and scenarios before discovery, scenario updates, or test authoring.

Update `tasks/qa-tasks.md` for substantive work. Propose routine work in `jobs/` and `cadence.md`.

Honor the execution gate: `npm run qa:review -- --gate`. Answer open items per `human-decides-loop.md`.

End sessions with `knowledge-curator`. Draft client scope via `scope-proposal` skill and `npm run qa:proposal`.

AI must not automatically change assertions, delete/skip tests, update baselines, redefine expected behavior, promote knowledge to confirmed, mark human review approved, send proposals externally, or hide failures.
